WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.464 --> 00:00:10.586
Research answers questions with sources. A researcher gathers and writes, a checker verifies every claim against its source, and only then is the note published.

2
00:00:11.290 --> 00:00:14.436
Open Research in the sidebar of a research project.

3
00:00:15.136 --> 00:00:24.817
New research card opens the card form. Give it a title, write the question the way you would ask a colleague, choose how deep to dig, and press Specify.

4
00:00:31.011 --> 00:00:40.216
Back on Research, In progress lists the open research cards and the stage each one is in. A blocked card waits for your answer on the desk.

5
00:00:40.921 --> 00:00:49.220
Published notes are the answers that passed the fact check, with a preview and every citation. Each citation links to its source.

6
00:00:49.921 --> 00:00:58.152
Each note is kept as a file in the project's vault folder, at the path under its title, so your team and your agents can find it later.

7
00:00:58.853 --> 00:01:03.543
That is Research: ask a question, and get a checked answer with its sources.
